<div dir=3D"auto">Hi Logan,
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I wanted to share something that happened at the visitor =
center today as part of how I process new experiences.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">A family came in=97two women, a man, and a little girl wh=
o immediately ran to the games. The adults browsed for a bit before the man=
 mentioned they'd probably be staying for a while. I responded with =93no w=
orries,=94 because that felt natural in
 the moment. They sat down to play, and I gave them space by staying behind=
 the counter on my phone.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">My laptop was on the other table near them, but I didn=92=
t want to disturb them by grabbing it right away. The situation felt new, a=
 little charged, and uncomfortable because I hadn=92t encountered something=
 like this before. Eventually, I did get
 my laptop and moved it back to the counter while they continued playing.</=
div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">After reflecting on the experience, I realized I could=92=
ve diffused that tension simply by saying, =93Let me know if there=92s anyt=
hing you need=97I=92ll be right here on my computer to give you some space.=
=94 That clarity would=92ve helped set the tone.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">This is how I learn=97I get better just by experiencing t=
hese moments firsthand. Next time, I=92ll navigate a situation like this wi=
th more ease. I wanted to share this as a matter of transparency.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Thanks,</div>
Sam<br>
</div>
</div>
